window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>\"He is off limits. Complicated. Not right for me at all. He's trouble, wrapped up in an expensive navy suit.</p> <p>But I never could stay out of trouble.\"</p> <p>Kat Canton is a woman with a plan. Though a rebel at heart, she’s had to stay focused since becoming a single mom at seventeen. She has been content to quietly chip away at her goals in a quirky little lake town in the Ozarks, despite her famous last name. Her daughter is thriving, her savings account is growing, everything is on track.</p> <p>Until she learns her dad’s business (the one funding said account) is in serious trouble.</p> <p>And the man hired to turn things around is the absolute worst.</p> <p>Dennis DeLane may be a genius with failing companies, but the billionaire is also a stiff, pompous, arrogant snob. Kat’s polar opposite, suddenly always around—at the restaurant, the inn, the coffee shop—with his gorgeous face and a deep British accent fit to narrate romance novels.</p> <p>He’s surprising. He’s infuriating. He’s invigorating. He’s also her cousin’s ex-fiance. So it’s a good thing his contract only lasts ninety days…This standalone novel is a smart, sexy, full-length contemporary romance. Prepare for laugh-out-loud banter, small town shenanigans, tension, twists, a swoony happily ever after, and a Canton group text thread you’ll wish you could join!</p>"; 
